I've found that one of the best ways to go from "lowly beginner" to {jbocre}
(lojban expert, not that I am one yet) is to try things that are too hard
for you and get corrected.  Read the CLL and the BPFK sections, try some
translations (first back from lojban, then into lojban), read Alice or The
Little Prince (I'll get around to them eventually).

There's nothing stopping you from trying to make new words; in doing so,
you'll learn to understand the process better, and we'll be able to correct
you.

